[0.067, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A• \u001b[1mLocation\u001b[m: \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk213677c0e08d4d53;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/data/repositories/parts_repository.dart#L162-L166\u0007PartsRepository._persist\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 & \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkad36d047755745c0;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/data/services/local_storage_service.dart#L72-L81\u0007FileLocalStorageService.savePartsJson\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[74D\u001b[1mIssue\u001b[m: Rapidly tapping the \u001b[94m+\u001b[m / \u001b[94m-\u001b[m buttons on \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk99ab80564e3c8b97;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/ui/features/inventory/views/parts_list_view.dart#L260-L263\u0007PartsListView\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 or \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk9527b2086c5decbe;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/ui/features/inventory/views/part_detail_screen.dart#L311-L355\u0007PartDetailScreen\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 triggers overlapping \u001b[94mfile.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mwriteAsString(..., flush: true)\u001b[m calls without serialization or debouncing"]
[0.0, "o", ", which can cause I/O race conditions or\r\n  corrupt writes.\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### 3. Logic & UX Issues\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mUnhandled \u001b[94;22merrorMessage\u001b[39;1m in UI\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkec13f59091cd5196;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/ui/features/inventory/view_models/inventory_view_model.dart#L39-L50\u0007InventoryViewModel.errorMessage\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 is set when \u001b[94mloadInventory\u001b[m, \u001b[94msavePart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mdeletePart\u001b[m, \u001b[94madjustQuantity\u001b[m, or\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mrenameLocation\u001b[m fails, but no widget ever reads or displays \u001b[94mviewModel.errorMessage\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[94m'Unassigned'\u001b[39;1m Location Filter Bug on Rename\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk28d4c391d1913588;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/ui/features/inventory/view_models/inventory_view_model.dart#L282-L285\u0007InventoryViewModel.renameLocation\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mif (_selectedLocation == oldLocation)\u001b[m checks against \u001b[94moldLocation\u001b[m. When\r\n\u001b[6Cas"]
[0.0, "o", "signing a location to \u001b[94m'Unassigned'\u001b[m parts from \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk6ca5bab4f5167bfd;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/ui/features/inventory/views/locations_view.dart#L60-L63\u0007LocationsView._showRenameLocationDialog\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94moldLocation\u001b[m is passed\r\n\t \u001b[94m''\u001b[m while \u001b[94m_selectedLocation\u001b[m is \u001b[94m'Unassigned'\u001b[m, so the active location filter is left pointing to \u001b[94m'Unassigned'\u001b[m.\r\n\u001b[6C• Additionally, if a user names a storage bin \u001b[94m\"Unassigned\"\u001b[m, it collides with the sentinel value used for empty\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mstorageLocation\u001b[m strings.\u001b[K\r\n  3. **Inaccurate Merge Count in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8624265ad4455f6b;file:///Users/brett/Demos/flutter-parts-experiment/parts_tracker_baseline/lib/ui/features/inventory/view_models/inventory_view_model.dart#L312-L325\u0007InventoryViewModel.importData\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007**:\r\n      • \u001b[94mreturn replaceExisting ? _allParts.length : (_allParts.length - beforeCount);\u001b[m returns \u001b[94m0\u001b[m when merging parts\r\n\u001b[6Cthat update exist"]
